  standing rule against new Rust/robot-control code and this task's explicit design brief
  (operations coordination, not direct trenching/heavy-equipment operation or
  utility-tie-in/energization-authorization authority): no robotics/simphysics analog, no
  module committing a real-world actuation effect. Every proposal carries :effect
  :propose unconditionally; the governor HARD-holds anything else. Built by reading
  cloud-itonami-isic-4210 in full and adapting its module shape (utilconstr.* namespace)
  to the utility-line-construction domain, renaming the domain-specific forbidden-
  action-class markers from 4210's :finalizes-engineering-design?/:finalizes-grade-plan?
  to this actor's :finalizes-tie-in-authorization?/:finalizes-energization-
  authorization?, with clojure -M:test independently re-run before and after every push,
  matching the stricter verification protocol of the preceding ISIC-coverage batch (72+
  consecutive successes after an earlier 18-agent haiku batch had a 61% defect rate)."

 :scope-exclusions
 ["heavy-equipment control (excavators, trenchers, directional-boring rigs, cranes) --
   outside this actor's authority entirely; the closed op-allowlist cannot express it,
   and the governor's forbidden-action-class HARD check independently rejects any
   proposal carrying an :equipment-control?/:direct-actuation? marker, un-overridable by
   any human approval"
  "utility-tie-in / energization-authorization authority -- connecting a new
   water/sewer/gas/electric/telecom line to a live main, or starting flow/pressure/
   current on it -- the licensed utility engineer's / site supervisor's exclusively.
   :schedule-construction-operation proposes a trenching/pipe-laying/tie-in-crew phase
   window, never a finalized tie-in or energization decision; the same
   forbidden-action-class check rejects a :finalizes-tie-in-authorization?/:finalizes-
   energization-authorization? marker"
  "real-world actuation of any kind -- every committed record carries :effect :propose
   only (effect-not-propose HARD check, defense-in-depth against a compromised/
   malfunctioning advisor)"]

 :decision
 "Implement cloud-itonami-isic-4220 with Governor, Facts, Registry, Store, Notify,
  Advisor, Phase, Operation, Sim (structured after cloud-itonami-isic-4210
  module-for-module, narrowed/renamed to the utility-line-construction domain):
  - Governor (Utility-Construction Governor): 8 hard checks (unknown-op,
    effect-not-propose, forbidden-action-class [equipment-control/direct-actuation/
    tie-in-authorization-finalization/energization-authorization-finalization markers],
    site-not-verified, legal-basis-missing, utility-locate-incomplete,
    notification-lead-time-insufficient [quantitative jurisdictions only],
    unresolved-safety-concern) + high-stakes escalation (:flag-safety-concern and
    :schedule-construction-operation ALWAYS escalate unconditionally at every phase;
    :order-supplies escalates above a $5000 USD cost threshold or below the 0.6
    confidence floor)
  - Facts: per-jurisdiction (JPN/USA/DEU) excavation/buried-utility-strike-prevention +
    road-opening/utility-installation-permit legal-basis catalog, reusing the SAME real
    official-source citations cloud-itonami-isic-4210's already-verified catalog carries
    (Japan's 労働安全衛生規則第355条 + 道路法第32条/建設リサイクル法第10条 168-hour notice;
    USA's OSHA 29 CFR 1926.651(b) 24-hour floor + 23 CFR 645.213 utility
    use-and-occupancy permit [the most literally on-point citation in this whole fleet
    for this ISIC class] + 23 CFR 630 Subpart J/MUTCD Part 6; EU/Germany's Directive
    92/57/EEC Art.3 + StVO 45 Abs.6, honestly :qualitative), reframed for utility-line
    construction (these statutes govern excavation/buried-utility-strike prevention
    generically, so reuse is not fabrication). Pipeline-specific technical-safety
    regimes (USA 49 CFR Parts 192/195; Japan gas/electricity business act tie-in rules)
    honestly noted as real but out of scope for this R0 catalog -- exactly why the
    governor permanently blocks tie-in/energization-authorization proposals
  - Registry: pure-function site-record-log/schedule-proposal/safety-concern-flag/
    supply-order-proposal drafts (jurisdiction-scoped sequence numbering) +
    render-safety-concern-notice (human-readable document, legal basis inline,
    explicitly disclaims tie-in/energization-authorization authority)
  - Store: Store protocol, dual MemStore/DatomicStore (langchain.db), contract-tested
    for parity. DatomicStore uses langchain-store.core (ADR-2607141600). No history is
    double-actuation-guarded -- every op may recur any number of times per site
  - Notify: mail+phone (Resend+Twilio) Notifier protocol, structurally identical to
    roadrail.notify, fires only after human approval of :flag-safety-concern
  - Advisor: Advisor protocol + deterministic mock-advisor (default) + llm-advisor
    (real-inference seam), all four ops carry :effect :propose
  - Phase: 0->3 rollout gate; :log-site-record/:order-supplies are the ONLY ops ever in
    a phase's :auto set (phase 3); :schedule-construction-operation/:flag-safety-concern
    permanently absent from every phase's :auto set
  - Operation: langgraph-clj StateGraph actor, real interrupt-before human-in-the-loop +
    checkpoint resume, structurally identical to roadrail.operation
  - Sim: demo driver (clojure -M:dev:run), 8 seeded sites, full episode + all HARD-hold
    paths + cross-jurisdiction (USA) + qualitative (DEU/EU) walkthrough
  - Operations: log-site-record (utility-locate/trenching-progress data logging,
    auto-eligible), schedule-construction-operation (trenching/pipe-laying/tie-in-crew
    scheduling, ALWAYS escalates), flag-safety-concern (utility-strike/excavation-
    collapse/gas-leak, ALWAYS escalates), order-supplies (cost-threshold-gated)
  - Tests: 68 tests / 258 assertions, all green
  - All .cljc (portable, no JVM interop in src), AGPL-3.0-or-later
  - README/GOVERNANCE/CODE_OF_CONDUCT/CONTRIBUTING/SECURITY domain-adapted for
    utility-line-construction coordination"

